ORDER BY Clause — Sort rows
Sorts output ascending (ASC) or descending (DESC).

Syntax:
SELECT column_list
FROM table_name
ORDER BY column_name [ASC|DESC];

Example:
SELECT emp_name, salary
FROM employees
ORDER BY salary DESC;

ORDER BY Multiple Columns:
SELECT emp_name, dept_id, salary
FROM employees
ORDER BY dept_id ASC, salary DESC;

COMBINING WHERE and SORT:
SELECT emp_name, salary
FROM employees
WHERE salary > 50000
ORDER BY salary DESC;

LIMIT/FETCHING:
Returns top 5 highest-paid employees
SELECT emp_name, salary
FROM employees
ORDER BY salary DESC
LIMIT 5;

USAGE OF ALIAS IN SORTING AND FILTERING:
SELECT emp_name, salary * 12 AS annual_salary
FROM employees
WHERE salary * 12 > 600000
ORDER BY annual_salary DESC;

ORDER OF SQL Execution:
| Step | Clause   | Description         |
| ---- | -------- | ------------------- |
| 1    | FROM     | Get data from table |
| 2    | WHERE    | Filter rows         |
| 3    | GROUP BY | Group rows          |
| 4    | HAVING   | Filter groups       |
| 5    | SELECT   | Select columns      |
| 6    | ORDER BY | Sort rows           |
| 7    | LIMIT    | Restrict output     |

This explains why you can’t use column aliases in WHERE — they’re created after WHERE executes.


| Clause         | Purpose            | Example                             |
| -------------- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| WHERE          | Filter rows        | `WHERE salary > 50000`              |
| AND / OR / NOT | Combine conditions | `WHERE dept_id=10 AND salary>60000` |
| BETWEEN        | Range filter       | `WHERE salary BETWEEN 40K AND 80K`  |
| IN             | Match list         | `WHERE dept_id IN (10,20)`          |
| LIKE           | Pattern match      | `WHERE emp_name LIKE 'A%'`          |
| IS NULL        | Check nulls        | `WHERE manager_id IS NULL`          |
| DISTINCT       | Remove duplicates  | `SELECT DISTINCT dept_id`           |
| ORDER BY       | Sort rows          | `ORDER BY salary DESC`              |
| LIMIT / TOP    | Restrict count     | `LIMIT 5`                           |

